-- title:
--   Folding a cancelling pair of consecutive boundary darts
-- statement:
--   For permutations $r,f$ of a finite set $A$, let $\mathrm{cyc}$ count cycles (fixed points included) and $\mathrm{comp}(r,f)$ count the classes of the equivalence relation generated by both. The pair is a planar map if
--   $$
--   \mathrm{cyc}(r)+\mathrm{cyc}(f)+\mathrm{cyc}(rf)=|A|+2\,\mathrm{comp}(r,f),
--   $$
--   i.e. equality holds in the Euler bound. Let $r$ be a fixed-point-free involution, $(r,f)$ planar, with labels in an alphabet with involutive flip, $\mathrm{label}(rz)=\mathrm{flip}(\mathrm{label}(z))$, colours constant along $rf$, and $\mathrm{color}(e)\ne\mathrm{color}(\mathrm{flip}\,e)$. Let $a\ne b$ with $f(b)=a$ and $\mathrm{label}(a)=\mathrm{flip}(\mathrm{label}(b))$. Then $r'=\mathrm{rePair}(r,a,b)$ and $f'=(b\ \ f(a))\,f$ give a planar labelled map with the same compatibility conditions, in which
--   $$
--   r'a=b,\quad r'b=a,\quad f'a=b,\quad f'b=a .
--   $$
--   Moreover $f'$ agrees with $f$ away from $b$ and $f(a)$, and the components of $(r',f')$ refine those of $(r,f)$.
--
--   The two folded darts become an isolated component, and the rest of the outer word is unchanged.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/GroupTheory/Hyperbolic/RePairing.lean#L435-L496

